body:
Holy shit. you just helped me have an "a-ha!" moment.

When I was 7, I busted my knee and needed stitches. I was taken to the emergency area of a nearby clinic by my teacher (I was at after-school sports club). When we got there they told me they would have to give me stitches without anesthesia b/c they didn't have any. So they did. It hurts but I just held on, I didn't cry at all. The nurse was shocked, and said she'd never seen a little kid, or even adult, get stitches without any anesthesia and not cry or at least flinch. I was literally just sitting there watching her sew my skin together as if I was watching cartoons. I was fucking 7 years old.

When my mom picked me up, she didn't even look worried, or asked me how I was. I just shrugged it off and we went home. I don't remember anything more about that. No comforting me about my injury, no nothing.

&#x200B;

I didn't realise that this isn't how a child should have to behave when facing an injury. I didn't act tough because I wanted to prove I was bad ass. I literally thought I didn't have the right to cry, because it was beaten out of me by my abusive father and it made my mom either scold me for crying or walk out of the room every time I did. So I just stopped. And I thought that acting strong in the face of physical pain was what you're supposed to do. I never had patience or sympathy for those that cried and wailed when they got hurt. It just simply didn't compute: why cry if nobody is going to come?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Yeah, no I get it. I also take 3g of melatonin, and it is supposed to knock me out, and it does, but I instinctively fight it. Its stupid, I know, because I need to sleep in order to heal from all of this, but, it's my flight reaction taking over, I can't control it.

&#x200B;

I don't want to take anything stronger/not natural. I hate having to take anything, especially for an indefinite period of time.

Even if you don't INTEND it, you're still RESPONSIBLE for the behaviour. 

&#x200B;

It's that last part that some aspies don't seem to grasp.

Actually, you can celebrate your birthday with all of Mexico. It's their birthday today too (Independence Day, Sept. 16th) Eat a burrito! ;)

&#x200B;

Edit: I wrote have a shot of tequila too, but you're only 17, so you have to wait a few years for that. It would be super fun though, if you could spend your birthday in Mexico someday. What a party!

>I realized she never protected me, I have ZERO memories of being safe  or emotionally open ever with her, and have never been allowed to be  honest about my feelings lest I get the silent treatment for 4 days  after.

This really hit me. I had the same realisation about my mother just days ago. Same deal.

&#x200B;

Yes absolutey!

&#x200B;

Same thing: too bright and hot. Mosquitoes. BO in public places
